WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.949
Bill Denbrough is the brave leader of the
Loser’s Club that fights Pennywise to avenge

00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:08.189
his brother Georgie, but in the book, Bill
isn’t written to be as much of a good person

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:11.840
as he is in the movies, stick around to the
end of this video to find out why.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:21.900
IT, the ancient evil that terrorized Derry,
Maine, singled out one individual opponent

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.650
above all others, and that was Bill Denbrough.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.130
Bill was the leader of the Loser’s Club,
a name given to the group of 12 years olds

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:32.370
who decided to take on It by the town bully,
Henry Bowers.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:37.550
My name is Andy Muschietti and today on Horror
History we’ll be covering the main protagonist

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.510
of IT and his short-lived little brother:
Georgie.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.789
Despite his speech crippling stutter, Bill
was probably the bravest character in the

00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:46.280
book, but he wasn’t always that way.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:51.020
To understand how Bill came to be, let’s
take it back to the birth of Big Bill.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:58.820
In 1946, Derry hydro-electric worker Zack
Denbrough, and classical pianist Sharon Denbrough

00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:03.489
gave birth to their first son, William, who
would eventually go by a nickname: Bill.

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:07.550
At a young age, Bill was in a minor car accident,
which his mother believed was the cause of

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:10.220
his stutter, but it’s unclear if that is
actually true.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:13.830
Bill had a very close relationship with his
parents when he was young, and that bond was

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:19.030
only strengthened when Zack and Sharon gave
birth to their second son, George, in 1951.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:23.390
Though they did not always get along, Bill
cared deeply for George; and George loved

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.120
and looked up to his older brother.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.240
In October of 1957, when Georige was 6, Bill
was sick in bed and used this free time to

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.410
make a papercraft boat for his brother to
play with in the rain.

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:36.930
Georgie was thrilled that his brother would
do this for him, and took special care not

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:40.510
to lose the boat, so when the current swept
it away to the intersection of Wicham and

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.960
Jackson street, Georgie took after it.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.800
The boat fell into a storm drain, and Georgie
was disappointed to lose the boat that his

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.090
brother had worked so hard to make for him.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:54.120
Then, he heard a voice inside of the drain
and saw a man in clown makeup standing there.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.270
The man introduced himself as Pennywise and
tried to get Georgie to come down into the

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:02.170
sewers with him by offering balloons, cotton
candy and rides.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:07.050
Georgie said he has to go, but when Pennywise
showed him the boat he decided to stay for a little bit longer.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:11.800
When you’re down here with me, you’ll
float too!” the clown told Georgie as he

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:16.629
reached for it, and Pennywise ripped off his
arm, ending the boy’s life prematurely at

00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:18.129
age 6.

00:02:18.129 --> 00:02:20.620
This event had a huge effect on Bill for the
rest of his life.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.900
And this feeling stuck

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.519
with him even after he had forgotten how his
brother had died.

00:02:25.519 --> 00:02:29.040
In December that same year, Bill snuck into
Georgie’s old room to look at his photo

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:33.139
album, and thought he saw something move in
one of the photos, but still wasn’t sure

00:02:33.139 --> 00:02:34.490
if it was his imagination.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:38.109
Georgie’s death had a negative effect on
Bill’s relationship with his parents.

00:02:38.109 --> 00:02:41.939
His mother gave up playing the piano after
Georgie’s funeral, and the void he sat in

00:02:41.939 --> 00:02:46.150
between his parents when they all sat on the
couch together felt longer and colder without

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:48.099
Georgie also there next to him.

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:51.730
One day, his parents got into a fight when
his father tried to remove the toys out of

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:55.549
Georgie’s room, and they both ended up sobbing
in separate rooms, paying no attention to

00:02:55.549 --> 00:02:57.240
how this was affecting Bill.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.219
One could come to the conclusion that because
of this awkward home life, Bill started spending

00:03:01.219 --> 00:03:05.049
more time out of the house, and he became
pretty good friends with an asmatic kid named

00:03:05.049 --> 00:03:06.200
Eddie Kaspbrak.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.049
One day, 8 months after his brother’s funeral,
Bill and Eddie were playing in the Barrens

00:03:10.049 --> 00:03:14.650
when three bullies, Victor Criss, Belch Huggins
and Henry Bowers came running up to the embankment

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:16.769
and asked if they had seen a fat boy anywhere.

00:03:16.769 --> 00:03:20.420
The boys destroyed the dam that Bill and Eddie
had been building and beat up Eddie, giving

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:22.700
him a bloody nose and an asthma attack.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:26.690
After the bullies left, Bill meets the boy
that they were looking for, Ben Hanscom, and

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:29.169
asks if he’ll stay with Eddie while he goes
to try to get his medicine.

00:03:29.169 --> 00:03:32.749
He grabs his bike, Silver, who he’s named
after the horse from The Lone Ranger, and

00:03:32.749 --> 00:03:37.139
when he rides Silver, he becomes like a new
person, which resembles his adult self.

00:03:37.139 --> 00:03:41.049
He rides fast, but with reckless abandon,
and I think that without the power that silver

00:03:41.049 --> 00:03:43.719
holds, he would likely have been struck dead
in the traffic.

00:03:43.719 --> 00:03:47.889
Bill’s stutter is so bad, that he must write
request to the pharmacist on a piece of paper

00:03:47.889 --> 00:03:49.629
in order to get Eddie’s aspirator.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:53.629
When he gets back, they’re amazed at how
quickly he made the run, and Bill and Eddie

00:03:53.629 --> 00:03:57.859
become friends with Ben, bonding over their
beatings at the hands of Henry Bowers.

00:03:57.859 --> 00:04:00.760
That day, Bill decided to take another look
at Georige’s photo album.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:05.049
He’s been starting to have visions of Georgie
as a monster, which I think are a result of

00:04:05.049 --> 00:04:08.060
It trying to rattle Bill hoping he could be
a future target.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:11.859
Bill flips to Georgie’s school photo, and
it winks at him, causing him to drop the book,

00:04:11.859 --> 00:04:15.909
and blood drips out of the pages, though Bill’s
parents would not be able to see the blood.

00:04:15.909 --> 00:04:19.739
The next day Bill helps construct the dam
at the stream in the Barrens, and introduces

00:04:19.739 --> 00:04:22.250
Richie Tozier and Stan Uris to Ben.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:26.480
As they all relax by the stream bank, Bill
tells the group he needs to tell them something

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.150
serious, and tells the story about the photo
album.

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.300
This is part of what makes him the leader
of the group.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:35.180
They’ve all seen the influence of Pennywise,
but none of them are brave enough to acknowledge

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:37.960
it and talk about, because that makes it real.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:41.849
None of them, besides Bill, who musters up
the bravery because he’s sick of tip-toeing

00:04:41.849 --> 00:04:43.860
around the subject of his brother’s killer.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:47.820
Bill doesn’t know it’s related to Pennywise
or the murders at this point though, and thinks

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.730
it has something to do with Georgie’s ghost.

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:53.880
They are interrupted by Mr. Nell, the Irish
Cop, who tells them their dam is disrupting

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.450
the drainage system in Derry.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:58.789
Bill tries to take the blame, but each one
of them shares part of the blame.

00:04:58.789 --> 00:05:03.069
This is an indicator and Bill’s selflessness,
which comes into play for him later on.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:06.900
Bill and Richie walk home together, and Richie
asks if he can see the photo album.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:11.940
Bill originally says no, but after a heartfelt
conversation with Richie, he agrees, a small

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:15.470
hint about the power that the Losers Club
can gain when they are united.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:18.830
When they go into Georgie’s room, Richie
is able to see the blood stained pages.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:22.750
Georgie’s photo is missing, instead, there’s
a picture of downtown Derry from the olden

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:23.750
days.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:27.129
A pair of sailors walks down the street, and
they have Richie and Bill’s faces.

00:05:27.129 --> 00:05:31.520
The picture begins to move, and they turn
towards the canal, where a clown pops up from

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:34.919
over the edge like a jack-in-the-box, but
with Georgie’s face.

00:05:34.919 --> 00:05:39.020
He reaches towards the sailor Bill, and real
Bill reaches into the photo, before Richie

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.110
yanks his arm out, and Bill’s hand is bleeding.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:45.199
I’d interpret this as a warning sign from
It to Bill.

00:05:45.199 --> 00:05:48.940
He wants Bill to draw that association between
the murder of his brother and what he percieves

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:52.669
as the monster, because that’s going to
make Bill more afraid than he was before,

00:05:52.669 --> 00:05:54.830
and Pennywise feeds off of fear.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.159
However, Bill doesn’t shy away from the
challenge as It expects.

00:05:58.159 --> 00:06:02.550
Early on in the summer, Bill is not able to
join the others in seeing “I Was A Teenage

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.090
Werewolf” at the movie theater because he’s
busy taking a speech therapy test in Bangor.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:10.060
His mother would continually urge him to repeat
the phrase: “he thrusts his fists against

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:12.630
the posts, but still insists he sees the ghosts”.

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:16.330
This is something theater performers commonly
use to warm up, and it’s supposed to help

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:20.290
Bill overcome his stutter, but he’s also
able to use it to overcome other things, such

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:22.530
as fear, doubt or evil.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:26.220
So Bill misses the werewolf movie, but he
does get to experience the werewolf anyway,

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:30.330
when he and Richie go to investigate the abandoned
house at 29 Neibolt Street.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:33.870
Bill brings with a pistol that he stole from
his father, but it isn’t effective against

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.220
It, which uses the werewolf form and wears
a Derry High School jacket.

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:42.909
Bill accuses It of killing his brother, to
which It responds, “I’ll kill you too.”

00:06:42.909 --> 00:06:46.750
It ends up chasing them down the street, and
they try to escape on Silver, but It, now

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:50.210
in the form of the Clown, but still wearing
the Derry High School jacket continues to

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:53.690
gain ground on them until they get near a
busy street and It disappears.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:58.090
The event is traumatizing for Bill, but it
does give him a clue he needs to help take

00:06:58.090 --> 00:07:01.120
the fight directly to Pennywise.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:12.260
After the altercation at 29 Neibolt, Bill
and Richie looked back as they were escaping

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:16.180
on Silver, to discover that Pennywise had
just disappeared next to a storm drain.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:20.680
I think Bill was probably the only one who
could have put this together along the location

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:25.319
where his brother Georgie was found to determine
that It is somehow connected to the sewers.

00:07:25.319 --> 00:07:28.020
He asks his father, who works for Derry Hydroelectric

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:32.000
and he explains that the pipes are mostly
empty except for during the Spring floods.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:36.370
He also tells him to stay out of the sewers,
warning him that he could easily get lost

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:37.370
in there.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:40.810
Bill also does some research of his own, and
on July 3rd, after getting together with the

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:45.020
Losers at the Barrens he explains his findings;
that several other cultures seem to have different

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.139
versions of It.

00:07:46.139 --> 00:07:50.650
The Irish have a creature known as a Glamor,
the Plains Indians have the Manitou, the Himalayans

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:57.240
have the Talus (even though I thought that was only in Breath of the Wild), Central Europe has the Alack
and the French have the Lupe Garoo.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:01.210
He explains that the Himalayans used something
called “The Ritual of Chud” to defeat

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:02.210
their Talus.

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:05.729
They would overlap tongues, then bite in so
they’re stapled eye to eye.

00:08:05.729 --> 00:08:09.740
They must then tell jokes and riddles back
and forth, and the first to laugh loses.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:12.480
“The rule is simple.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:13.900
You laugh.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:15.320
You die.”

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:18.720
Actually, Felix is kind of right, and I think
I just died.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:26.919
If the human loses, he dies, but if the Talus
loses, he must go away for 100 years.

00:08:26.919 --> 00:08:30.780
So at this point Bill started gathering up
Tik-Tok videos to show Pennywise, during the

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:32.320
ritual…

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:34.380
OK -- I think I died again.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.650
On July 3rd, the losers get together to shoot
off some firecrackers, but Bill tells them

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:41.160
to put them away because he senses something
is going to happen.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:44.790
I think this is Bill using The Shine, which
is the psychic clairvoyance that comes up

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:48.760
in a lot of Stephen King novels, most prominently
Danny Torrance from the Shining.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:52.390
I think they all probably shine a little,
but Bill’s is the strongest, and this actually

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:56.209
kind of ties into the reason he has to be
the one to perform the Ritual of Chud.

00:08:56.209 --> 00:09:00.510
He tells his to create a stash of rocks because
he feels like the Bowers and the bullies are

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:04.670
going to attack, and what ensues becomes known
as the Apocalyptic Rock Fight.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:09.269
Bill plays a big role in it by not flinching
away from the notorious fastball pitcher Victor

00:09:09.269 --> 00:09:12.510
Criss and hitting him with a rock that causes
him to run from the fight.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:16.089
The Losers talk more about how Pennywise could
be defeated as they build their new clubhouse

00:09:16.089 --> 00:09:20.070
in the Barrens that July, where Bill develops
a theory that they can kill the monster using

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:21.070
a silver bullet.

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:24.880
It’s something that works in the movies,
and as kids, they all believe that it actually

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.520
works and go to the library to research more
methods.

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:31.510
Bill also contributed to the completion of
the clubhouse by secretly borrowing some of

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:33.480
his father’s tools from the garage.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:36.920
After completing it, Mike Hanlon brings his
father’s old photo-book to show them how

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:40.850
Pennywise is scattered throughout Derry’s
history, and one of the pages comes to life

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:45.200
and Pennywise rushes them and hangs on a lampost
in the foreground, threatening to kill them

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:45.700
all.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:46.980
"I'll kill you all!"

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:49.820
Everyone is trauma-stricken by the encounter.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:53.250
Stan is so deeply affected that he goes into
denial about it even happening.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:56.570
But if you analyse Bill’s reaction, it’s
different than everyone else.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:10:01.320
Sure, he’s shaken up by what happened, but
he also feels that IT is scared of them.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:05.699
On July 17th, the Losers are seeking advice
on how to fight It, and they decide to perform

00:10:05.699 --> 00:10:08.240
this Indian Smoke Hole ritual in their clubhouse.

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:12.010
The idea was that they’d breath in the smoke
and have visions that would help them.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:16.660
I think the homeless population in LA has
a similar strategy, and I don’t think it

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:17.660
works.

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:20.240
As they’re trying to decide who’s going
to be the one to do it, Bill shows his leadership

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:24.019
and protectiveness of Beverly, by arguing
that it shouldn’t be her because she’s

00:10:24.019 --> 00:10:25.019
a girl.

00:10:25.019 --> 00:10:27.710
They all pick out a match, and whoever gets
the burned one is supposed to stay up top

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:32.010
to pull them to safety if anyone passes out,
however, they all pull matches, and none of

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:36.320
them are burned anymore, so they take the
hint and they all go into the smokehole.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:40.560
Bill stays in as long as he can and sees the
inside of the tiny clubhouse start to expand

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:44.160
to the size of a ballroom, but eventually
he can’t take it anymore and he’s is the

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.360
fifth one to jump out.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:48.750
Bill was definitely the biggest threat to
It, but it just goes to show that he wasn’t

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:51.269
strong enough without the shared power of
his friends.

00:10:51.269 --> 00:10:55.800
On July 20th, after Eddie got his arm broken
by Henry Bowers, Bill gathers up the gang

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:59.459
to go visit him at the hospital, where Eddie’s
overprotective mother ambushes them and tells

00:10:59.459 --> 00:11:00.459
them off.

00:11:00.459 --> 00:11:03.660
They wait out until that night to try again,
in the meantime, developing the plan to melt

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:06.829
down some silver dollars to use as ammo for
Bill’s slingshot.

00:11:06.829 --> 00:11:10.631
From what I understand silver dollars were
much bigger back then than they are now, so

00:11:10.631 --> 00:11:12.339
it actually could have been effective.

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:16.040
However, Bill himself wasn’t a great shot
with the slingshot

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:19.680
"You're in the lead right now with a pathetic 3/10"

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.140
"Richie, will ya please shut up?"

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:22.220
So it's decided that

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:24.100
Beverly will be the one to handle It.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:25.740
It was midway through the summer...

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:26.940
No... not that Midsommar.

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.520
when Beverly
approached the others in a panic after seeing

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:32.070
It take out one of the bullies, Patrick Hockstetter.

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:36.330
They go to investigate spot in the junkyard
where Beverly saw it happen and find a threat

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:38.480
from Pennywise written in blood.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:42.130
Maybe he had just had enough of being the
victim, or maybe his mind connected the sight

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:46.580
of Patrick’s blood with his own brother’s
but this is where Bill snapped and screamed

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:47.769
out, “we’re gonna kill you!”

00:11:47.769 --> 00:11:52.019
He asks his friends desperately for their
help and they all join together in a hug in

00:11:52.019 --> 00:11:53.019
the rain.

00:11:53.019 --> 00:11:56.650
Three days later, everyone goes to Bill’s
place so they can make the silver slugs, and

00:11:56.650 --> 00:12:00.870
although Ben was the one to physically make
them, Bill used his creativity to help them

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:04.440
get away with it without his parents finding
out by setting up a Monopoly board to make

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:07.410
it look like they were in the middle of a
game, which they could rush inside to sit

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:08.930
around when his parents came home.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:13.560
Two days later, they arrived at 29 Neibolt
Street for the first time since Bill and Richie’s

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:15.160
werewolf encounter earlier that summer.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:19.470
Bill’s bravery and determination to avenge
his brother caused him to lead them in crawling

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:22.730
under the porch, where they could climb in
through a basement window.

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:26.180
IT started to play tricks on them as they
made their way through one corridor.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.699
The hallway elongated.

00:12:27.699 --> 00:12:32.339
The eyes of the elves on the wallpaper started
to bleed and the ceiling closed in on them,

00:12:32.339 --> 00:12:34.070
causing everyone to freak out.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:37.470
Perhaps it was Bill’s strong shine that
allowed him to stay calm and realize what

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:38.720
they were seeing isn’t real.

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:42.550
He punches up to where the ceiling appeared
to be, and when he did so they could all see

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:46.050
that what they were seeing was not true, and
this fixes the room.

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:49.480
The others perceive Bill’s strength to be
a result of his love for his brother, but

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:53.880
he reminds them that they all have their own
quirks that help them fight back against It’s

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:54.880
manipulations.

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:58.170
Eventually they make it to a door, and Big
Bill is the first to approach it.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:01.660
He hears pumping machinery coming from the
other side, just like the sound of the pumping

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.990
stations, or as they call them, Morlock Holes,
in the Barrens.

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:08.440
I think Bill, with his knowledge of the Derry
hydroelectric system acquired from his father,

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:11.250
was the first to realize what was behind this
door.

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:12.960
This… was were It came from.

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:25.050
Behind the door was a dilapidated bathroom,
but this was no Saw movie, this was where

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:27.060
It connected to the world on the surface.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:30.259
They were attacked by It, once again in the
werewolf form.

00:13:30.259 --> 00:13:34.149
Beverly missed her first shot, and It sprang
at Bill, knowing he was the leader and seeing

00:13:34.149 --> 00:13:36.029
the chance to demoralize the group.

00:13:36.029 --> 00:13:39.980
Ben steps in front and It ends up slashing
Ben before Beverly hits it on her third and

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:44.319
final shot, causing It to scream death threats
at them as It retreated into the sewers.

00:13:44.319 --> 00:13:49.020
Beverly’s blouse is damaged, and Bill offers
her his shirt to cover up, once again showing

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:53.199
the seedlings of their attraction and Bill’s
protective nature, which we would see more

00:13:53.199 --> 00:13:56.339
of when everything went down a couple weeks
later.

00:13:56.339 --> 00:14:01.800
On a mysteriously quiet day in August, Richie,
Eddie and Stan run into Bill with his bike

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:03.060
in the middle of town.

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:07.110
Mike later shows up too and then all of the
sudden Ben and Beverly are running up to them,

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:10.760
telling of how Henry Bowers had snapped and
chased after Beverly, and were now skulking

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:12.010
about in the Barrens.

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:15.810
Bill makes the decision for the group, they’re
going to reclaim their play spot.

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:19.250
It was at this remark that Eddie started to
think that Henry wasn’t the only one who

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:22.529
was losing it, Bill was drifting towards madness
as well.

00:14:22.529 --> 00:14:26.430
If we analyse his character to this point,
he’s driven by the desire for revenge for

00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:30.170
his brother’s death, crippled by grief for
his friends and classmates and shaped by all

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:33.180
the adult situations he’s already had to
face at age 12.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:37.470
He’s even subconsciously ridden his bike
in a dangerous way through busy streets -- a

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:40.040
very subtle beginning of suicidal tendencies.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:44.560
So it’s likely that Eddie was right, and
Bill was starting to lose his sanity a little bit

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:48.930
that summer, but unlike Henry Bowers, Bill
was able to get a grip on it, and actually

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:51.910
use it to his advantage to write horror novels
as an adult.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:55.600
They go into the Barrens and get attacked
by rocks thrown by Victor and Belch.

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:59.750
At this point Bill realizes that It is the
biggest source of what’s wrong with Derry,

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:02.819
and asks Ben to lead them to the pumping station
that connects to the sewer.

00:15:02.819 --> 00:15:06.399
Eddie’s arm is still broken, so Bill carries
him on his back down the ladder.

00:15:06.399 --> 00:15:10.270
They shake Henry Bowers and go into the inflow
pipe underground, an image that would stick

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:14.279
with Bill through the years and end up in
one of his horror novels: The Black Rapids.

00:15:14.279 --> 00:15:18.670
They venture into the dark in a line, keeping
one hand on the shoulder of the person in

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:23.310
front of them to stay together and unknowingly
following the path of the paper boat Bill

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:25.840
made for Georgie almost a year ago now.

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:28.990
They come across a small door leading to the
lair of It.

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:32.870
Bill is unable to see It’s true form and
interprets it as a giant spider.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:35.220
Bill is the one to cross the room towards
the spider.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:38.269
It tells him that It is eternal, an eater
of worlds.

00:15:38.269 --> 00:15:42.730
Bill is heaved across the chamber, into the
blackness, the cosmos of the universe.

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:47.329
He faced off against It on something described
as “the ballroom floor of eternity.”

00:15:47.329 --> 00:15:51.600
He was thrust by It, deep into the macroverse
-- and although Georgie’s physical form

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:55.890
had long since deceased, he could feel his
brother had a place in the Macroverse.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:59.730
Bill was caught by another celestial force
called the Turtle, who didn’t want to engage

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:04.399
in the dispute, but did give Bill the advice
he needed, by telling him to thrust his fists

00:16:04.399 --> 00:16:08.380
against the posts, and still insist he sees
the ghosts -- the speech therapy technique

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:10.300
that Bill could often be heard using.

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:13.629
The Ritual of Chud doesn’t happen in the
movie, but there is little reference to this

00:16:13.629 --> 00:16:14.629
line.

00:16:14.629 --> 00:16:21.900
“He thrusts… his fists… against the
posts… and still insists… he sees the

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:23.320
ghosts…

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:26.260
He thrusts his fists against the p-p..."

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:32.700
As the 
human voice of It fades out, the alien language

00:16:32.709 --> 00:16:35.720
of the deadlights, the true form of it, fades
in.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:40.470
Bill establishes a mental connection by biting
into It’s metaphysical tongue and using the

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:43.040
“teeth of his mind” and begins the Ritual
of Chud.

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:46.759
Although Bill should not have been able to
stand a chance, it was his belief in all of

00:16:46.759 --> 00:16:50.730
the childish things he believes in -- like
the silver bullets, the power of his bike,

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:53.920
and the phrase “he thrusts his fists against
the posts and still insists he sees the ghosts”

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:58.740
and helped him overcome It, causing it to
scream and beg for Bill to let go.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:02.329
They return to the real world, where It retreats
further into the chamber.

00:17:02.329 --> 00:17:06.590
The losers decide that it sounded like it
was dying, but Bill is unsure what to think.

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:10.289
They try to flee before the pipes fill up
with rainwater and drown them, but get lost

00:17:10.289 --> 00:17:14.650
on the way out, and Bill remembers his father
warning, to never play in the sewers because

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:18.270
it would be easy to get lost, but eventually
they do make their way out of the sewers,

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:19.860
where the sky is starting to clear up.

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:23.959
This would be the last time all 7 of them
were ever together in the same place at the

00:17:23.959 --> 00:17:28.020
same time again, and the leader of the Losers
Club would make one more request that would

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:30.510
forever change the course of their lives.

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:34.630
He asks them to promise that if It were ever
to come back, no matter where they were, they

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:36.470
would return and try to kill It again.

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:41.070
They make a blood pact, before breaking off
one by one and returning home.

00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:44.900
When Bill leaves, he thinks he never wants
to play in the Barrens again.

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:49.380
Just like when Bill would ride on Silver,
defeating It opened the gates towards adulthood.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:53.780
Over the next year, Bill would lose his stutter,
and it was gone by the age of 13.

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:56.000
One by one, the group moved out of Derry.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:18:00.000
Bill attended a college in Maine to study
literature, listing influences like Edgar

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.700
Allen Poe, HP Lovecraft, and Richard Matheson.

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:06.909
He’s a C student, occasionally able to earn
a B. One day he calls out his pretentious

00:18:06.909 --> 00:18:10.400
instructor in front of the class.“Why does
a story have to be socio-anything?

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:15.830
Politics… culture… history… aren’t
those natural ingredients of any story if

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:16.830
it’s told well?”

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:20.270
“I mean, can’t you guys just let a story
be a story?”

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:21.400
You know what Bill?

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:24.840
Yes…. but I’m still not gonna delete my
channel.

00:18:24.840 --> 00:18:28.890
The instructor has a much ruder reaction though,
humiliating him in front of the class and

00:18:28.890 --> 00:18:31.830
suggesting that he has a great deal to learn.

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:35.630
That week, Bill writes a story called “The
Dark” about a small boy who kills the monster

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:36.670
lurking in his cellar.

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:40.570
I’m not sure if he realizes he’s told
his own story about defeating the monster

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:44.580
under Derry and downscaled it to the single
house level, because at this point some of

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:48.510
his memories about Derry, Georgie and It have
already started to fade.

00:18:48.510 --> 00:18:53.559
The teacher gives him and F and calls it “pulp
crap” so Bill decides to send it to a magazine

00:18:53.559 --> 00:18:55.240
where it receives praise.

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:59.039
He sends the feedback to his instructor alongside
his drop card.

00:18:59.039 --> 00:19:01.780
During his senior year, he writes a novel
and gets it published.

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:04.809
At the age of 23, he’s already a successful
writer.

00:19:04.809 --> 00:19:09.650
He starts dating his agent, Susan Browne and
works on a second novel called The Black Rapids,

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:13.830
which he sells the movie rights to and has
the option to do the first draft of the screenplay,

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:16.590
after which he is invited out to Hollywood
for further rewrites.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:20.460
Susan begs him not to go, but he ends up leaving
Maine for the West Coast.

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:24.940
An actress named Audra Phillips is cast in
the movie and Bill ends up marrying her.

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:27.070
He would go on to write more novels.

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:31.180
Based on the titles of his books, I think
they are all a result of the horrifying experiences

00:19:31.180 --> 00:19:34.700
he had as a child: The Dark and The Black
Rapids could be about the journey through

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:39.200
the sewers, The Glowing refers to The Deadlights,
the true form of It, though that one could

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:40.789
also be a parody of The Shining.

00:19:40.789 --> 00:19:44.451
There’s also a werewolf novel whose title
is not mentioned, which could come from the

00:19:44.451 --> 00:19:46.310
Werewolf form of It that they battled.

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:50.340
He also has an original screenplay called
Attic Room, possibly about the encounter he

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:52.370
had at 29 Neibolt Street with the others.

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:57.110
Bill’s life is going great, he’s successful,
he’s married to a superstar, and he’s

00:19:57.110 --> 00:20:00.600
long forgotten about the traumatic childhood
in Derry.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:05.960
All is well until 1985, when his old buddy
Mike Hanlon calls him up on the phone while

00:20:05.960 --> 00:20:10.180
Bill is shooting a movie in England with some
horrible news.

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:10.840
It… has returned!

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:23.151
After Mike fills Bill in on everything remnants
of his childhood re-emerge in the 39 year

00:20:23.151 --> 00:20:24.350
old Bill Denbrough.

00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:28.190
His stutter comes back, scars appear on his
hands where the blood pact was made and he

00:20:28.190 --> 00:20:32.169
remembers for the first time in years, how
his little brother Georgie truly died, but

00:20:32.169 --> 00:20:34.620
not all of the memories come back right away.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:38.720
He abandons the production to board a plane
to the US, and suddenly it seems apparent

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:42.620
that the inspiration for all of his horror
novels was Derry.

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:46.350
On the cab ride over from his hotel to the
restaurant they’re all meeting at Bill’s

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:50.110
apologetically foul mouthed cabbie, who by
the way is probably my favorite character

00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:54.030
in the book and deserves his own episode of
Horror History, points out how Derry has become

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.790
more of a small city over the years.

00:20:55.790 --> 00:21:00.080
By this point, everyone already knows about
how Stan offed himself, but when he enters

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:04.861
the room with the 5 remaining Losers Club members,
Bill feels like there is a 6th somehow, perhaps

00:21:04.861 --> 00:21:08.900
a clue that despite losing most of his memories
about his childhood, he seems to have retained

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:09.900
a little bit of his “shine”.

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:13.080
And no, I’m not talking about his now bald
head.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:16.539
Mike starts explaining about the murders that
caused him to believe that It was back, and

00:21:16.539 --> 00:21:20.910
when he tells about the death of Adrian Mellon,
Bill is the only one to realize that the one

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:25.260
who pulled up his body, Harold Gardner, was
the son of Dave Gardner, the man who found

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.260
Georgie.

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:29.780
Mike also tells of another death where police
found a photograph of Georgie is found near

00:21:29.780 --> 00:21:33.880
the body, and Bill realizes it’s the same
photo that disappeared from the album when

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:34.880
he was a kid.

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:38.860
At the end of the meal, Bill gets a bad feeling
about the fortune cookies, which I found similar

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:41.720
to the bad feeling he got before the rock
fight in 1958.

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:45.039
The contents of each of their cookies is specific
to their fears.

00:21:45.039 --> 00:21:49.460
Bill doesn’t open his but he can tell it’s
a mutant fly, like from the George Langlahan

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:51.200
story, “The Fly”, which scared Bill a
lot.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:53.120
Do we have a clip of the movie?

00:22:00.560 --> 00:22:04.330
Mike has them walk the town to try to regain
some of their old memories, and Bill meets

00:22:04.330 --> 00:22:08.320
a kid with a skateboard who tells him he heard
changing voices coming from one of the pipes near

00:22:08.320 --> 00:22:10.700
a pumping station and warns him to stay away.

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:14.390
The kid seems surprised that Bill is privy
to the thing that haunts Derry.

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:17.960
I think Bill and his friends are unlike other
adults in town because they made the promise

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:18.960
in 1958.

00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:23.789
Bill asks to try to kid’s skateboard, but
at the last second decides not to, and the

00:22:23.789 --> 00:22:27.030
scene is symbolic of how Bill no longer has
the childlike energy that got him through

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:28.820
the encounter with It the first time.

00:22:28.820 --> 00:22:33.000
He continues walking, then asks a little girl
what her favorite store in Derry is and she

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:35.470
tells him it’s Secondhand Rose, Secondhand
Clothes.

00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:39.380
He goes over and sees his old bike, Silver,
in the window, and for the first time in a

00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:43.669
long time, he thinks about the phrase, “he
thrusts his fists against the posts and still

00:22:43.669 --> 00:22:45.059
insists he sees the ghosts.”

00:22:45.059 --> 00:22:48.440
After buying the bike, he gets permission
to store it at Mike’s house and together,

00:22:48.440 --> 00:22:50.760
they fix up the bike, adding childish frills,
like playing cards.

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:52.000
Adding Childifsh....

00:22:52.360 --> 00:22:53.400
Adding childsh

00:22:53.400 --> 00:22:55.120
I sound like ****ing Bill right now...

00:22:55.120 --> 00:22:58.280
They fix up the  bike, adding childish frills like playing cards.

00:22:58.490 --> 00:23:03.390
Mike opens a new pack of cards and it contains
two Ace of Spades, one with a blue back and

00:23:03.390 --> 00:23:06.049
the other red, as if was a mixed deck.

00:23:06.049 --> 00:23:09.740
I think this represents the elements of Bill’s
childhood starting to manifest themselves

00:23:09.740 --> 00:23:13.940
in the adult Bill, similar to how his stutter
and old scars came back.

00:23:13.940 --> 00:23:17.850
This night, after and catching up with everyone
some more at the library over drinks, and

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:21.169
after having another scary encounter with
It, who uses the form of Stan Uris’s head

00:23:21.169 --> 00:23:24.390
to threaten the Losers Club, they call it
a night -- starting to feel better about their

00:23:24.390 --> 00:23:27.510
chances after recovering more of their lost
memories.

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:31.480
Before leaving, Beverly starts screaming about
their hands, and they realize all of their

00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:34.400
hands are bleeding from the scars where they
made the promise.

00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:38.810
They all hold hands as crazy supernatural
occurrences rock the library, and Bill gets

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:42.520
the feeling that this would be the last time
all 6 of them were together, just like the

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:46.580
promise they made in 1958 was the last time
the seven were together.

00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:50.220
After this happens, Beverly claims she now
remembers everything that happened in the

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:54.870
original battle with It, and Bill is dismally
aware that he was falling in love with Bev.

00:23:54.870 --> 00:23:57.510
The two decide to walk back to the hotel together.

00:23:57.510 --> 00:24:01.799
Beverly asks for a kiss, and Bill becomes
aware of how much she looks like Audra and

00:24:01.799 --> 00:24:02.799
kisses her.

00:24:02.799 --> 00:24:07.270
I can give Bev a pass, because she just left
an abusive husband, but pretty uncool on Bill’s

00:24:07.270 --> 00:24:08.270
part.

00:24:08.270 --> 00:24:11.200
They end up going back to Bill’s room and
they go all the way.

00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:14.320
Obviously, this is a pretty crappy thing to
do on Bill’s part, but in terms of what

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:18.169
it means for his character, he’s realizing
that the woman he married is very much like

00:24:18.169 --> 00:24:20.020
one of his first attractions when he was younger.

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:21.940
OK, that sounds weird to say.

00:24:21.940 --> 00:24:26.659
What I’m trying to say is that Bill realizes
he never lost the youthful energy and mindset

00:24:26.659 --> 00:24:30.360
that helped him defeat It, just like how his
creative mind was a big part of his childhood

00:24:30.360 --> 00:24:34.929
and he became a writer to continue channeling
that energy even after he had forgotten about

00:24:34.929 --> 00:24:35.929
Derry.

00:24:35.929 --> 00:24:38.669
Bill gets a call from Eddie’s room in the
middle of the night, and show up to find his

00:24:38.669 --> 00:24:42.679
arm broken once again, and Henry Bowers dead
in the hotel room.

00:24:42.679 --> 00:24:46.789
They realize It must have broken out Henry
and decide they can’t wait until tomorrow,

00:24:46.789 --> 00:24:50.010
they have to kill It tonight, before one of
them gets killed.

00:24:50.010 --> 00:24:54.169
They call over to the library to tell Mike,
but the police chief picks up -- they were

00:24:54.169 --> 00:24:55.169
too late.

00:24:55.169 --> 00:24:57.049
Henry had put Mike in the hospital.

00:24:57.049 --> 00:25:01.690
The remaining five of them pile into Eddie’s
limo where It taunts Bill over the car radio.

00:25:01.690 --> 00:25:05.800
Each one of them had fears as children, and
each of them have new fears as adults, but

00:25:05.800 --> 00:25:10.070
Bill’s fear has stayed constant -- he fears
losing someone he loves ever since he lost

00:25:10.080 --> 00:25:11.280
his brother, Georgie.

00:25:11.280 --> 00:25:16.390
It uses Geogie’s voice, screaming things
like “you let it kill me!” to rattle Bill.

00:25:16.390 --> 00:25:20.130
This wouldn’t be the only thing It did to
expose Bill’s fear though.

00:25:20.130 --> 00:25:24.550
When they arrived at the manhole Bill finds
a familiar object, it’s his wife Audra’s

00:25:24.550 --> 00:25:25.550
purse!

00:25:25.550 --> 00:25:29.600
She had come after him, against his warnings,
and It had abducted her, knowing that Bill

00:25:29.600 --> 00:25:31.669
just couldn’t handle losing another loved
one.

00:25:31.669 --> 00:25:32.669
I mean…

00:25:32.669 --> 00:25:35.240
I would say he shouldn't have cheated on her
if that was the case… but…

00:25:35.240 --> 00:25:36.780
I’m not supposed to have an opinion.

00:25:36.780 --> 00:25:40.990
Bill once again has to carry the cripled Eddie
down the ladder, just as they did as children.

00:25:40.990 --> 00:25:45.090
The sewer systems have changed over the years,
but the old unused pipes are still in place

00:25:45.090 --> 00:25:49.280
and the five members of the Losers make their
way back to the lair of It, but there would be

00:25:49.280 --> 00:25:51.000
one more challenge for Bill

00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:51.760
before they get there.

00:25:51.760 --> 00:25:56.880
get there. There were instances back in 1958 where It
threatened Bill with one of his worst fears,

00:25:56.909 --> 00:26:00.590
claiming it would take the form of George
in order to drive Bill insane.

00:26:00.590 --> 00:26:05.570
However, unlike the movie, It saves this trump
card for the sewers in 1985.

00:26:05.570 --> 00:26:11.470
Bill held up his match and saw Georgie approaching
him in his yellow rain jacket, crying and

00:26:11.470 --> 00:26:12.659
looking for his boat.

00:26:12.659 --> 00:26:19.020
When Georgie cried, a strange garble of sounds
was heard, but Bill was too heartbroken to

00:26:19.020 --> 00:26:20.760
notice that something was off.

00:26:20.760 --> 00:26:22.710
Bill felt he deserved to die.

00:26:22.710 --> 00:26:26.650
All the others can do is encourage Bill to
realize it’s not really Georgie and fight

00:26:26.650 --> 00:26:27.650
it.

00:26:27.650 --> 00:26:31.250
Bill’s stutter is hampering not only his
speech, but his rationality, but he’s finally

00:26:31.250 --> 00:26:39.520
able to successfully recite the line: “he
thursts his fists against the posts but still

00:26:39.520 --> 00:26:46.429
insists he sees the ghosts,” to overcome
both his stutter and It, which retreats back

00:26:46.429 --> 00:26:47.429
into the inner lair.

00:26:47.440 --> 00:26:52.520
There was only one thing left to do now: the
final confrontation with It.

00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:05.250
As Bill, Ben, Eddie, Richie and Beverly get
into the spider’s chamber, they realize

00:27:05.250 --> 00:27:09.700
that they no longer needed the matches, as
there is something emanating from it.

00:27:09.700 --> 00:27:10.700
The Deadlights.

00:27:10.700 --> 00:27:15.320
The nightmarish spider descends from above
and Bill finds Audra strung up in the webbing.

00:27:16.440 --> 00:27:21.760
"They float Georgie.."

00:27:21.760 --> 00:27:25.760
Bill confronts the spider and finds himself
being flung out of his physical body and back

00:27:25.770 --> 00:27:26.770
into the void.

00:27:26.770 --> 00:27:31.030
It tells him that the Turtle, who helped him
in 1958, died a few years ago and won’t

00:27:31.030 --> 00:27:32.480
be of any use this time.

00:27:32.480 --> 00:27:36.590
It threw him again, and Bill tried to mentally
seize It’s tongue to engage in the Ritual

00:27:36.590 --> 00:27:39.240
of Chud, but this time he misses his grip.

00:27:39.240 --> 00:27:43.039
Back in the actual physical chamber, Richie
notices Bill’s face contorting.

00:27:43.039 --> 00:27:47.240
His spirit is in another realm, so Richie
runs up to the spider and tries to distract

00:27:47.240 --> 00:27:49.630
it, but he to it whacked into the macroverse.

00:27:49.630 --> 00:27:51.230
Richie is able to engage in the Ritual.

00:27:51.230 --> 00:27:55.789
Richie takes Bill’s hand and they hold tightly
onto It, which returns to the real world and

00:27:55.789 --> 00:27:57.710
they get back to their physical bodies.

00:27:57.710 --> 00:28:01.950
When they arrive, they find that the spider
has already maimed Eddie, and he’s dying,

00:28:01.950 --> 00:28:05.309
but this time they can’t let It get away
and they follow it into the deepest part of

00:28:05.309 --> 00:28:06.309
the chamber.

00:28:06.309 --> 00:28:10.090
The deadlight is leaking out of It now, and
it begs them to let it go, offering them the

00:28:10.090 --> 00:28:14.470
chance to live for 500 years, but Bill, with
his child-like innocence only wants to see

00:28:14.470 --> 00:28:16.460
his brother’s killer brought to justice.

00:28:16.460 --> 00:28:21.409
It’s only fitting that over 27 years later,
Bill is the one to punch his was into the

00:28:21.409 --> 00:28:24.799
spider’s chest and crush his heart with
his bare hand.

00:28:24.799 --> 00:28:28.670
After helping Richie back to the others, Bill
finds his wife and discovers she still has

00:28:28.670 --> 00:28:31.029
a pulse, but she’s become catatonic.

00:28:31.029 --> 00:28:35.140
Eddie is dead, and without him, they have
a much harder time navigating their way out.

00:28:35.140 --> 00:28:39.170
Bill is the one to eventually realize there
is light coming in through small holes in

00:28:39.170 --> 00:28:40.200
the top of the pipe.

00:28:40.200 --> 00:28:43.780
The street above them had collapsed in the
epic flood that took place while they were

00:28:43.780 --> 00:28:47.570
fighting It and they are able to pull themselves
up onto Main Street.

00:28:47.570 --> 00:28:51.360
Beverly tells Bill that she hopes Audra is
going to be alright, and they share one last

00:28:51.360 --> 00:28:56.440
hug, which is photographed by a reporter documenting
the damage and appears in the newspaper with

00:28:56.460 --> 00:28:58.080
the caption: survivors.

00:28:58.110 --> 00:29:01.870
Audra is taken away in an ambulance, and Bill
runs into the skateboard kid from before and

00:29:01.870 --> 00:29:03.480
tells him it’s alright now.

00:29:03.480 --> 00:29:07.570
At first, this seems like an insignificant
interaction, but I can only imagine how good

00:29:07.570 --> 00:29:12.019
this felt for Bill, after being driven to
destroy the monster under Derry for so long

00:29:12.019 --> 00:29:15.980
because of what happened to his brother to
let the new young generation know they don’t

00:29:15.980 --> 00:29:17.340
have to be afraid anymore.

00:29:17.340 --> 00:29:21.409
With IT dead, the remaining Loser’s club’s
memories started to fade once more, this time

00:29:21.409 --> 00:29:23.160
much faster than before.

00:29:23.160 --> 00:29:28.059
Within a few days, Bill was unable to remember
Stan’s last name, or Eddie’s health condition.

00:29:28.059 --> 00:29:30.130
Bill had one last thing to take care of.

00:29:30.130 --> 00:29:32.590
Audra was released from the hospital before
Mike.

00:29:32.590 --> 00:29:36.650
She was able to eat solid foods now, but she
was still catatonic, so Mike let them stay

00:29:36.650 --> 00:29:40.970
at his house to try to rehab, but she wasn’t
making much progress, and Bill began to fear

00:29:40.970 --> 00:29:42.760
his wife would be a vegetable forever.

00:29:42.760 --> 00:29:47.580
He had one more idea to try to save her, something
that had saved him, something that had saved

00:29:47.580 --> 00:29:49.279
Eddie and Richie too.

00:29:49.279 --> 00:29:51.179
His old bike: Silver.

00:29:51.179 --> 00:29:55.950
Decked out with all of his childhood fanfare
like the playing cards, basket and horn, he

00:29:55.950 --> 00:30:01.210
sat Audra in the carrier and did what he had
always done, rode fast and recklessly downhill

00:30:01.210 --> 00:30:05.480
into a busy street, picking up speed instead
of braking -- and just like his belief in

00:30:05.480 --> 00:30:10.560
everything from his childhood saved him once
before against It, Audra comes to and hold

00:30:10.570 --> 00:30:14.750
onto Bill, whose stutter has completely disappeared
and they embrace.

00:30:14.750 --> 00:30:18.970
Bill was the centerpiece of the Loser’s
Club that finally defeated the scourge of

00:30:18.970 --> 00:30:21.660
Derry, Maine, laying IT to rest.

00:30:21.660 --> 00:30:25.840
His bravery and leadership shined through
even the bleakest of scenarios, and he was

00:30:25.840 --> 00:30:31.330
driven all along by his love for those close
to him: his wife Audra, before that his best

00:30:31.330 --> 00:30:36.220
friends Eddie, Richie, Stan, Ben, Beverly
and Mike, and through everything… his little

00:30:36.220 --> 00:30:37.220
brother Georgie.

00:30:37.220 --> 00:30:40.750
So that’s the entire known history of Bill
Denbrough.

00:30:40.750 --> 00:30:44.899
Your homework is to let me know in the comments
who I should analyse next on Horror History

00:30:44.899 --> 00:30:47.870
and click the playlist on the left for my
lessons on other characters.

00:30:47.870 --> 00:30:53.440
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, RING that deathbell for

00:30:53.440 --> 00:30:56.790
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:30:56.790 --> 00:30:59.090
Assuming we both survive.

